  "title": "The Smallest Abelian Cayley Graphs with a Goemans–Linial Gap",
  "batch_label": "66",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "proved",
  "scope": "For every admissible finite Abelian Cayley presentation in source.md, the least group order for which psi(G) > SDP_GL(G) is 10. Every admissible presentation of order at most 9 is exact. The 16 group-automorphism orbits of admissible presentations on Z_10 give 16 pairwise nonisomorphic graphs, and exactly three are non-exact: S={1,3,7,9}, with (psi,SDP_GL)=(4/5,3/4); S={1,4,6,9}, with (psi,SDP_GL)=(4/5,(15+sqrt(5))/22); and S={1,2,5,8,9}, with (psi,SDP_GL)=(5/6,(10+sqrt(5))/15). Thus these are precisely the three order-ten non-exact graph-isomorphism classes, and each has one Cayley-presentation orbit.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
